  "notes": "Swedish OpenStack cloud (Elastx AB, Stockholm). Single region se-sto (Stockholm) with three availability zones sto1/sto2/sto3; all prices are for this region. Prices published in SEK excl. VAT and billed per hour (CloudKitty metering). Converted to EUR at the ECB reference rate of 2026-10-30 (1 EUR = 10.9780 SEK); original SEK prices kept per instance in price_sek_hourly / price_sek_monthly_published. price_monthly = SEK hourly x 730 / rate. The page displays hourly prices rounded to 3-4 significant digits, so its own SEK monthly figures can differ by up to ~0.5% (e.g. g1-c24-m380-d3.2k-g160: 72 SEK/h x 730 = 52,560 SEK vs 52,800 SEK published). v1 = shared compute nodes (Intel Xeon Gold/Platinum), v2 = shared compute nodes (AMD EPYC 9634), d2/d3 = dedicated compute nodes (Intel E-2278G/E-2378G, AMD EPYC 7443P). v1 flavors are still listed without a deprecation note and are included; note that small v1 flavors are cheaper than the equivalent v2 flavors. All flavors include a local NVMe SSD boot disk (size in flavor name). GPU flavors (A100, L4, L40S, RTX PRO 6000) in gpu_instances. Managed Kubernetes (Kubernetes CaaS): 4,900 SEK/month (= control_plane_cost in EUR) as management fee on top of the infrastructure; non-managed CaaS 0 SEK. A cluster always runs 3 control-plane nodes (v2-c2-m8-d80, one per AZ) plus at least 3 worker nodes; per the Kubernetes pricing page the minimum cluster (router, load balancer, 3 control-plane + 3 worker v2-c2-m8-d80 nodes) costs ~5,000 SEK/month in infrastructure, i.e. control-plane nodes are billed as normal instances (3 x 834 SEK = 2,502 SEK/month) in addition to the 4,900 SEK fee. Managed tier includes 24x7 support, monitoring, up to 4 upgrades per year, scaling during office hours; backups not included. Cluster ordering and scaling is a manual process via sales/support (typically delivered within one business day); smaller dev/test clusters are possible but without the service terms. Additional network costs: router 0.6781 SEK/h (495 SEK/month), part of the minimum Kubernetes setup; Barbican secrets 0.13 SEK/h each. Discounts for 1- or 3-year commitments and volume tiers exist but are not public. Backups not priced."
